<p>As you know, some computers require additional controller driver(s) that=
 Microsoft does not add to the repository, <br>because of incompatibility b=
etween different versions. This is for example, Intel RST VMD Controller Dr=
iver, etc. <br>In WinPE, we do the installation of the driver(s) needed for=
 a particular computer, at boot time. <br>Now, if an additional driver is n=
eeded and installed, it will also be copied to the folder at the path X:\Lo=
calStorageDrivers. <br>That is, if you see the LocalStorageDrivers folder i=
n the root of disk X, it means that it contains the driver you need for the=
 computer you booted on. <br>This was added to WinPE x64, and was done main=
ly for ease of installation of a new OS. <br>When installing an operating s=
ystem, for example with the WinNTSetup program, you can specify this folder=
 with the driver(s) right in the program window. <br>Or install by any othe=
r available method, such as DriverStore Explorer program, etc. <br>This is =
convenient for example when you are unfamiliar with the computer, which sav=
es you time searching for the right driver.</p>
